<div style="color:#111111;" class="rounded p-6 gap-3 bg-light text-dark" data-zesty-id="content:wysiwyg_basic:2:71"><h5 style="text-align:center;">Our Children are Our Future</h5>

<p>
	Some of our most vulnerable community members are our youngest, and when there is a need, The Salvation Army does everything it can to help secure a brighter future for our children. Throughout the year, The Salvation Army supports area children through:
</p>

<p>
	<strong>B+ esl (English as second language classes) after school program</strong> – This is a free after school program focusing on children with limited English skills. Homework assistance and English classes, along with gym activities, crafts and more are offered throughout the school year.
</p>

<p>
	<strong>Summer Camp in New Orleans</strong> – Running from June 1 to August 1, the Corps hosts fun and creative outdoor and indoor activities for children. Registration begins in April; $25 per child to register with a weekly camp fee of $50 per child. Fee includes lunch and two snacks daily. Scholarships are available.
</p>

<p>
	<strong>Overnight summer camp at Camp Hidden Lake near Lexington, Mississippi</strong> - The Salvation Army’s 300-acre Camp Hidden Lake helps disadvantaged boys and girls in Alabama, Louisiana, and Mississippi develop new skills, healthy attitudes, and great values. Camp Hidden Lake offers sports, music, Bible Study, arts and crafts, swimming, fishing, and other activities for school-aged youngsters in our community.
</p>

<p>
	We also have a number of <a href="/new-orleans/worship" target="">youth programs</a> through the New Orleans Citadel Corps, or The Salvation Army church.
</p></div>
